  "notes": [
    "-AR verb with a spelling change: **z→c before e** to preserve the /s/ (Latin America) or /θ/ (Spain) sound. This affects the yo form of the pretérito indefinido (avancé, not *avanzé) and every form of the subjuntivo presente and the usted/nosotros/ustedes imperative forms (avance, avancemos, avancen).",
    "No stem change — purely an orthographic adjustment.",
    "Past participle is regular: **avanzado**.",
    "*Expósito deberá avanzar a través de corazonadas.* (\"Expósito will have to advance through hunches.\")",
    "*Avanzamos mucho en el proyecto esta semana.* (\"We made a lot of progress on the project this week.\")",
    "Related: *el avance* (advance/progress, noun), *avanzado/a* (advanced, adjective), other -zar verbs share this pattern (rechazar, abrazar, cruzar, esbozar)."
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/a/Avanzar.md"
